  h3/h3_arch/
    A hand port of ComfyUI v0.33.0's `comfy/ldm/minimax/` and
    `comfy/text_encoders/{minimax,qwen3vl,qwen35,llama}.py`. ComfyUI is
    GPL-3.0. `h3/h3_arch/text_encoder.py` states the adaptation in its own
    module docstring; `h3/h3_arch/__init__.py` states it for the package.

    These files are NOT covered by this repository's MIT LICENSE, and the two
    terms are not compatible. The honest description of the current state is
    that the repository carries a licence its own contents contradict.

    This is known and is being resolved by REMOVAL rather than by argument.
    Decision #593 deleted the incomplete alternate implementation: it had no
    bound artifact and could not execute the endpoint's conditioning/decode
    contract. The port is retained as the one graph the current release binds
    and has output-proven. A future official transition must produce and bind
    its exact artifact, implement and output-prove every operation, then add
    official and delete this port in the same release. `scripts/h3-oracle.py`
    imports a ComfyUI checkout on a rented card and is never imported by any
    endpoint or shipped in any release artifact.

    The current H3 project wheel DOES include `h3_arch`: it is the release's only graph,
    layout, presentation, and vision implementation. Public distribution remains blocked
    until an output-proven replacement and this directory change atomically; there is no
    conditional packager that can make the current source something it is not.


